<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Forms – review, login, feedback & validation</title>
  <style>
    * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
      font-family: system-ui, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif;
    }
    body {
      background: linear-gradient(145deg, #f7f9fc 0%, #eef2f7 100%);
      margin: 0;
      padding: 2rem 1.5rem;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: center;
    }
    .form-card {
      background: white;
      max-width: 680px;
      width: 100%;
      border-radius: 28px;
      padding: 1.8rem 2.2rem 2.2rem;
      margin-bottom: 2rem;
      box-shadow: 0 20px 35px -10px rgba(0, 20, 30, 0.15);
      border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6);
      transition: transform 0.1s ease;
    }
    .form-card:hover {
      box-shadow: 0 22px 40px -12px rgba(0, 40, 60, 0.2);
    }
    h2 {
      font-size: 1.75rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      margin-top: 0.2rem;
      margin-bottom: 1.6rem;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 0.5rem;
      color: #0b2a3c;
      letter-spacing: -0.01em;
      border-left: 7px solid #f97316;
      padding-left: 1rem;
    }
    h2 i {
      font-style: normal;
      font-size: 1.8rem;
    }
    .form-group {
      margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
    }
    label {
      font-weight: 600;
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
      color: #1e3b4f;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 6px;
    }
    .required-star {
      color: #dc2626;
      font-weight: 700;
      font-size: 1.1rem;
      line-height: 1;
    }
    input, textarea, select {
      padding: 0.8rem 1rem;
      border: 1.5px solid #d9e2ec;
      border-radius: 16px;
      font-size: 1rem;
      background: #fbfdff;
      transition: 0.2s;
      width: 100%;
    }
    input:focus, textarea:focus {
      outline: none;
      border-color: #f97316;
      box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px rgba(249, 115, 22, 0.15);
      background: white;
    }
    textarea {
      min-height: 110px;
      resize: vertical;
    }
    button {
      background: #0b2a3c;
      color: white;
      border: none;
      padding: 1rem 1.8rem;
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      border-radius: 40px;
      cursor: pointer;
      transition: 0.15s;
      margin-top: 0.6rem;
      width: 100%;
      letter-spacing: 0.01em;
      box-shadow: 0 6px 14px rgba(11, 42, 60, 0.2);
    }
    button:hover {
      background: #1a405a;
      transform: scale(1.01);
    }
    button:active {
      transform: scale(0.98);
    }
    .radio-group, .checkbox-group {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 1.2rem 2rem;
      margin: 0.5rem 0 0.2rem;
      padding: 0.25rem 0;
    }
    .radio-option, .checkbox-option {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 0.5rem;
      font-weight: 500;
      color: #1e3b4f;
    }
    .radio-option input, .checkbox-option input {
      width: auto;
      margin: 0;
      accent-color: #f97316;
      transform: scale(1.15);
    }
    .inline-hint {
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      color: #5a6e7e;
      margin-top: 0.4rem;
      background: #f2f6fa;
      padding: 0.3rem 0.8rem;
      border-radius: 20px;
      display: inline-block;
    }
    .explain-box {
      background: #e8f0fe;
      padding: 1.5rem 2rem;
      border-radius: 24px;
      margin-top: 0.8rem;
      border-left: 8px solid #f97316;
      color: #1a3449;
      font-size: 1rem;
      line-height: 1.6;
    }
    .explain-box strong {
      color: #b45309;
    }
    .badge {
      background: #f97316;
      color: white;
      border-radius: 60px;
      padding: 0.2rem 1rem;
      font-size: 0.8rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      letter-spacing: 0.3px;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      margin-left: 0.7rem;
    }
    hr {
      border: none;
      border-top: 2px dashed #cbd5e1;
      margin: 1.5rem 0 0.5rem;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <!-- 1. Food review form – POST method, name, email, comments -->
  <div class="form-card">
    <h2><i>🍽️</i> Restaurant review <span class="badge">POST</span></h2>
    <form action="foodReview.html" method="POST">
      <div class="form-group">
        <label for="reviewerName">Your name <span class="required-star">*</span></label>
        <input type="text" id="reviewerName" name="reviewerName" placeholder="e.g. Ananya Sharma" required>
      </div>
      <div class="form-group">
        <label for="reviewerEmail">Email address <span class="required-star">*</span></label>
        <input type="email" id="reviewerEmail" name="reviewerEmail" placeholder="you@example.com" required>
      </div>
      <div class="form-group">
        <label for="comments">Comments / review</label>
        <textarea id="comments" name="comments" placeholder="Tell us about the food, service, ambience…"></textarea>
      </div>
      <button type="submit">Submit review</button>
    </form>
  </div>

  <!-- 2. Music streaming login form – password type, required fields -->
  <div class="form-card">
    <h2><i>🎧</i> Music login</h2>
    <form action="#" method="post">
      <div class="form-group">
        <label for="musicUser">Username <span class="required-star">*</span></label>
        <input type="text" id="musicUser" name="username" placeholder="your_username" required>
      </div>
      <div class="form-group">
        <label for="musicPass">Password <span class="required-star">*</span></label>
        <input type="password" id="musicPass" name="password" placeholder="••••••••" required>
      </div>
      <button type="submit">Log in</button>
    </form>
  </div>

  <!-- 3. Movie booking feedback – radio (1-5 stars) + checkboxes for features -->
  <div class="form-card">
    <h2><i>🎬</i> Movie booking feedback</h2>
    <form action="#" method="post">
      <!-- Radio: rate experience 1-5 -->
      <div class="form-group">
        <label>Rate your experience (1–5 stars) <span class="required-star">*</span></label>
        <div class="radio-group">
          <label class="radio-option"><input type="radio" name="rating" value="1" required> ⭐ 1</label>
          <label class="radio-option"><input type="radio" name="rating" value="2"> ⭐ 2</label>
          <label class="radio-option"><input type="radio" name="rating" value="3"> ⭐ 3</label>
          <label class="radio-option"><input type="radio" name="rating" value="4"> ⭐ 4</label>
          <label class="radio-option"><input type="radio" name="rating" value="5"> ⭐ 5</label>
        </div>
      </div>
      <!-- Checkboxes: features used -->
      <div class="form-group">
        <label>Which features did you use?</label>
        <div class="checkbox-group">
          <label class="checkbox-option"><input type="checkbox" name="features" value="seat_selection"> Seat selection</label>
          <label class="checkbox-option"><input type="checkbox" name="features" value="food_order"> Food order</label>
          <label class="checkbox-option"><input type="checkbox" name="features" value="payment"> Payment</label>
          <label class="checkbox-option"><input type="checkbox" name="features" value="trailer"> Trailer / preview</label>
          <label class="checkbox-option"><input type="checkbox" name="features" value="loyalty"> Loyalty points</label>
        </div>
      </div>
      <button type="submit">Send feedback</button>
    </form>
  </div>

  <!-- 4. Email input that only accepts @gmail.com (pattern) + short explanation -->
  <div class="form-card">
    <h2><i>📧</i> Gmail-only input</h2>
    <form action="#" method="post">
      <div class="form-group">
        <label for="gmailOnly">Email (must end with @gmail.com)</label>
        <input type="email" id="gmailOnly" name="gmailEmail" 
               pattern="[a-zA-Z0-9._%+-]+@gmail\.com" 
               placeholder="username@gmail.com"
               title="Please enter a valid Gmail address (e.g., name@gmail.com)">
        <span class="inline-hint">pattern="[a-zA-Z0-9._%+-]+@gmail\.com"</span>
      </div>
      <button type="submit">Submit Gmail</button>
    </form>
  </div>

  <!-- 5. Explanation: front-end vs server-side validation -->
  <div class="form-card" style="background: #ffffff;">
    <h2><i>⚖️</i> Validation: front-end vs server-side</h2>
    <div class="explain-box">
      <p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1.2rem;">
        <strong>Front-end validation</strong> (HTML attributes like <code>required</code> and <code>pattern</code>) 
        runs in the browser and gives instant feedback — it improves user experience and reduces 
        unnecessary server round-trips. <br>
        <strong>Server-side validation</strong> happens after the form is submitted; it re-checks all data 
        on the server, which is essential because anything from the client can be bypassed, 
        disabled, or spoofed.
      </p>
      <p style="margin-bottom: 0;">
        <strong>Risk of relying only on front-end:</strong> A malicious user can disable JavaScript, 
        edit the HTML, or use tools like Postman to send invalid or dangerous data (e.g., SQL injection, 
        script tags, or an empty required field) directly to your server. Without server-side validation, 
        that bad data can be stored or executed, compromising security and data integrity.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

</body>
</html>
